     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (for example, 850 mg three times daily). A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg for immediate-release tablets. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas this a typo? Possible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max daily dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, such as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
      }
     ],
